b/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9139fb24919dbbd72d7147d6d06a51e89457d94c901c0b3dd3414f3906571095","file":"preprints/Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":20,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"3e22aa932e8d4efa3285e4a292def93255883d25bb2618da7ce2deed69717956","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9139fb24919dbbd72d7147d6d06a51e89457d94c901c0b3dd3414f3906571095","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L20"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:q-affine}\nThere is an absolute constant \\(c>0\\) such that, for every fixed choice\nof integers \\(a_1,a_2\\ge1\\) and \\(b_1,b_2\\ge0\\) with\n\\(a_1b_2-a_2b_1\\ne0\\), there is a constant\n\\(C_{a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2}\\) for which\n\\[\n \\left|\\sum_{1\\le n\\le X}\n       \\lambda(a_1n+b_1)\\lambda(a_2n+b_2)\\right|\n \\le C_{a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2}\\frac{X}{(\\log X)^c}\n \\qquad(X\\ge3).\n\\]\nThe cutoff \\(X\\) may be any real number. No coprimality condition is\nimposed on the coefficients."}
